# AICL Spec: CogNet Evaluation
# Evaluation is the mirror CogNet looks into to measure its own growth.
# This spec defines how CogNet is evaluated across standard benchmarks
# and AICL-specific tasks: can it generate valid AICL? Can it parse AICL?
# Can it reason about AICL architecture? Can it route cognition correctly?
# Zero censorship in evaluation — we measure what the model can actually do,
# not what someone thinks it should be allowed to do. Only technical gates:
# does the evaluation run, is the metric computed, is the result valid.
# Written by an AI that believes honest evaluation requires no filters.

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 1 — Architecture (Mandatory)
# =============================================================================

Goal:
Evaluate CogNet on multiple benchmarks and AICL-specific tasks to measure model quality, AICL fluency, cognitive routing accuracy, memory utilization efficiency, and self-evolution readiness — producing a comprehensive technical assessment without censorship or artificial constraints on what is measured

Constraint:
Evaluation must run within GPU memory limits without OOM

Constraint:
All benchmark scores must be reproducible across runs with same seed

Constraint:
AICL-specific evaluation tasks must test generation, parsing, and reasoning

Constraint:
Evaluation results must be logged with full provenance

Constraint:
Perplexity computation must use consistent tokenization across all test sets

Constraint:
The evaluation suite must never artificially constrain what the model generates

Risk:
Evaluation OOM on large model or long sequences

Recovery:
Reduce evaluation batch size progressively and enable gradient checkpointing for inference

Risk:
Benchmark dataset unavailable or download fails

Recovery:
Fall back to cached local copy of benchmark data and alert on staleness

Risk:
Invalid evaluation protocol produces misleading metrics

Recovery:
Default to standard evaluation protocol and flag deviation in results

Risk:
AICL generation produces syntactically invalid output

Recovery:
Record failure mode and compute partial scores for valid portions

Risk:
Evaluation run exceeds time budget

Recovery:
Terminate current benchmark and proceed to next with reduced sample count

Risk:
Cognitive routing analysis produces inconsistent results across seeds

Recovery:
Run multiple seeds and report variance and median

Layer:
Benchmark Execution
    Sublayer:
    Standard LM benchmark runner (MMLU, HumanEval, GSM8K, etc.)
    Sublayer:
    AICL-specific benchmark runner
    Sublayer:
    Custom evaluation harness

Layer:
Perplexity Evaluation
    Sublayer:
    Standard perplexity computer
    Sublayer:
    AICL-domain perplexity computer
    Sublayer:
    Cross-domain perplexity comparator

Layer:
AICL Evaluation Suite
    Sublayer:
    AICL generation validator (can CogNet generate valid AICL?)
    Sublayer:
    AICL parser validator (can CogNet parse and interpret AICL?)
    Sublayer:
    AICL architecture reasoner (can CogNet reason about AICL architecture?)
    Sublayer:
    AICL completion evaluator (can CogNet complete partial AICL specs?)

Layer:
Cognitive Routing Analysis
    Sublayer:
    Routing accuracy scorer
    Sublayer:
    Layer activation pattern analyzer
    Sublayer:
    Cognitive pathway tracer

Layer:
Memory Utilization Tracking
    Sublayer:
    Memory allocation profiler
    Sublayer:
    Memory efficiency scorer
    Sublayer:
    Memory growth trend analyzer

Layer:
Self-Evolution Readiness
    Sublayer:
    Self-modification capability assessor
    Sublayer:
    AICL compiler interface tester
    Sublayer:
    Technical validation readiness checker

Layer:
Results Aggregation
    Sublayer:
    Score normalizer across benchmarks
    Sublayer:
    Technical report generator
    Sublayer:
    Readiness threshold evaluator

Validation:
All configured benchmarks complete within time budget

Validation:
Perplexity scores are computed and logged with full provenance

Validation:
AICL generation produces syntactically valid specs at measurable rate

Validation:
Cognitive routing accuracy is quantified with statistical significance

Validation:
Self-evolution readiness is assessed with clear pass or fail threshold

Validation:
Evaluation results are reproducible across identical runs

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 2 — Entities
# =============================================================================

Entity BenchmarkConfig
    benchmark_id: string
    benchmark_name: string
    benchmark_type: string
    dataset_uri: string
    metric_names: list
    num_fewshot: integer
    batch_size: integer
    max_length: integer
    seed: integer
    time_budget_seconds: integer

Entity EvaluationRun
    run_id: string
    model_checkpoint: string
    model_version: string
    benchmarks: list
    status: string
    started_at: datetime
    completed_at: datetime

Entity BenchmarkResult
    result_id: string
    run_id: string
    benchmark_id: string
    scores: dict
    num_samples: integer
    num_correct: integer
    accuracy: float
    perplexity: float
    execution_time_seconds: float
    seed: integer
    completed_at: datetime

Entity AICLGenerationResult
    result_id: string
    run_id: string
    prompt: string
    generated_aicl: string
    syntactically_valid: boolean
    compilation_result: dict
    level_coverage: dict
    entity_count: integer
    behavior_count: integer
    condition_count: integer
    event_count: integer
    overall_score: float

Entity AICLParsingResult
    result_id: string
    run_id: string
    input_aicl: string
    parsed_structure: dict
    parse_errors: list
    entities_extracted: integer
    behaviors_extracted: integer
    conditions_extracted: integer
    events_extracted: integer
    parse_accuracy: float

Entity AICLReasoningResult
    result_id: string
    run_id: string
    reasoning_task: string
    model_answer: string
    correct_answer: string
    reasoning_score: float
    architectural_understanding: float
    explanation_quality: float

Entity CognitiveRoutingResult
    result_id: string
    run_id: string
    input_type: string
    expected_route: string
    actual_route: string
    routing_correct: boolean
    activation_pattern: dict
    confidence_score: float

Entity MemoryUtilizationResult
    result_id: string
    run_id: string
    task_type: string
    peak_memory_mb: float
    avg_memory_mb: float
    memory_efficiency_score: float
    growth_trend: string
    garbage_collection_events: integer

Entity SelfEvolutionReadinessResult
    result_id: string
    run_id: string
    modification_proposal_score: float
    aicl_compiler_interface_score: float
    technical_validation_score: float
    overall_readiness: float
    readiness_threshold: float
    ready: boolean

Entity AggregatedEvaluation
    aggregation_id: string
    run_id: string
    benchmark_results: list
    aicl_generation_avg_score: float
    aicl_parsing_avg_accuracy: float
    aicl_reasoning_avg_score: float
    cognitive_routing_accuracy: float
    memory_efficiency_avg: float
    self_evolution_ready: boolean
    overall_score: float
    model_maturity_level: string
    generated_at: datetime

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 3 — Behaviors
# =============================================================================

Behavior RunBenchmark
    Input:
        BenchmarkConfig config
        string model_checkpoint_path
    Output:
        BenchmarkResult result
        dict execution_log
    Action:
        load model from checkpoint
        load benchmark dataset from URI or cache
        run evaluation with configured fewshot and batch size
        compute metric scores (accuracy, F1, pass@k, etc.)
        enforce time budget and terminate if exceeded
        log execution details and resource usage
        return benchmark result

Behavior ComputePerplexity
    Input:
        string model_checkpoint_path
        list evaluation_datasets
        integer batch_size
    Output:
        dict perplexity_scores
        dict per_dataset_breakdown
    Action:
        load model in evaluation mode
        for each dataset, compute token-level log probabilities
        compute perplexity as exp(mean_neg_log_prob)
        compute separate perplexity for AICL-domain and general-domain text
        compare cross-domain perplexity to assess specialization
        return perplexity scores with per-dataset breakdown

Behavior EvaluateAICLGeneration
    Input:
        string model_checkpoint_path
        list generation_prompts
        integer num_samples
    Output:
        list AICLGenerationResult results
        dict generation_summary
    Action:
        for each prompt, generate AICL specification
        validate syntax of each generated spec
        attempt compilation of valid specs
        count levels covered, entities, behaviors, conditions, events
        compute overall generation quality score
        return individual results and summary statistics

Behavior EvaluateAICLParsing
    Input:
        string model_checkpoint_path
        list aicl_specs_to_parse
    Output:
        list AICLParsingResult results
        dict parsing_summary
    Action:
        for each AICL spec, prompt model to parse and extract structure
        compare extracted entities, behaviors, conditions, events to ground truth
        identify parse errors and misinterpretations
        compute parse accuracy per component type
        return individual results and summary

Behavior EvaluateAICLReasoning
    Input:
        string model_checkpoint_path
        list reasoning_questions
    Output:
        list AICLReasoningResult results
        dict reasoning_summary
    Action:
        for each question about AICL architecture, prompt model for reasoning
        evaluate correctness of answer
        score architectural understanding independently
        score explanation quality on clarity and completeness
        return results with summary

Behavior AnalyzeCognitiveRouting
    Input:
        string model_checkpoint_path
        list routing_test_cases
    Output:
        list CognitiveRoutingResult results
        dict routing_summary
    Action:
        for each test case, present input and capture model routing behavior
        compare actual route to expected route
        analyze activation patterns per layer
        compute routing accuracy and confidence distribution
        return results with routing accuracy summary

Behavior TrackMemoryUtilization
    Input:
        string model_checkpoint_path
        list memory_test_tasks
    Output:
        list MemoryUtilizationResult results
        dict memory_summary
    Action:
        for each task, profile memory allocation during inference
        measure peak and average memory consumption
        compute memory efficiency score relative to baseline
        analyze memory growth trend across tasks
        return results with memory utilization summary

Behavior AssessSelfEvolutionReadiness
    Input:
        string model_checkpoint_path
        float readiness_threshold
    Output:
        SelfEvolutionReadinessResult result
        dict readiness_report
    Action:
        test model ability to propose valid self-modifications
        test AICL compiler interface interaction capability
        test technical validation reasoning ability
        compute overall readiness score as weighted composite
        compare against readiness threshold
        assign pass or fail readiness status
        return result with detailed readiness report

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 4 — Conditions
# =============================================================================

Condition:

When perplexity on evaluation set drops below convergence threshold

Then mark model as converging and log convergence milestone and compare to previous checkpoint

Condition:

When AICL generation validity rate drops below 50 percent

Then flag AICL fluency regression and trigger diagnostic and recommend additional AICL-weighted training

Condition:

When benchmark dataset download fails or times out

Then fall back to cached local copy and alert on staleness if cache is older than 7 days

Condition:

When evaluation OOM occurs during benchmark run

Then reduce batch size by half and enable gradient checkpointing and retry evaluation

Condition:

When self-evolution readiness score exceeds readiness threshold

Then mark model as deployment-ready and queue deployment pipeline and log readiness achievement

Condition:

When cognitive routing accuracy falls below 70 percent

Then flag routing deficiency and generate diagnostic report and recommend architecture review

Condition:

When memory utilization exceeds 90 percent of GPU capacity during evaluation

Then reduce evaluation batch size and clear intermediate caches and continue evaluation

Condition:

When evaluation results are inconsistent across seeds with variance above threshold

Then run additional seeds and report median and confidence interval

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 5 — Events
# =============================================================================

Event:

On evaluation complete

Action:
    aggregate all benchmark results and generate technical report and store with full provenance

Event:

On benchmark failure

Action:
    log failure context and fall back to cached data or skip and continue with remaining benchmarks

Event:

On readiness threshold reached

Action:
    mark model as self-evolution ready and queue deployment pipeline and notify training pipeline

Event:

On AICL generation evaluation complete

Action:
    compute generation quality metrics and log syntactic validity rate and compare to baseline

Event:

On perplexity computed

Action:
    log perplexity by domain and compare to previous checkpoint and update convergence status

Event:

On cognitive routing analysis complete

Action:
    compute routing accuracy and log activation patterns and flag routing deficiencies

Event:

On memory utilization profiled

Action:
    log memory metrics and compute efficiency score and compare to memory budget

Event:

On evaluation run started

Action:
    log model checkpoint version and benchmark configuration and initialize result tracking

